comparing an int64 to an INLINE untyped negative const-expression (var n int64 = -42; n == 0 - 42) is miscompiled on the 32-bit ARM backend -- the negative const-expr is not widened to 64 bits before the compare so the high word mismatches and the equality is wrongly false (prints FAIL). n == -42 (a literal) and comparison via an int64 var both work on arm32; only the inline int64-vs-negative-const-expr form fails. spec const.int.sign (§6.3); claude-todo MAJOR (arm32 int64 const-expr compare).
